The plate is a square dinner plate, roughly 26 cm across. The food, which looks like scrambled eggs, covers about 160 px of the plate's roughly 450 px width. That works out to about 9 cm by 8 cm, or a small pile a few centimeters high.

For volume, a pile of about 9 × 7 cm at roughly 2.5 cm high comes to about 100–150 mL. Scrambled egg weighs about 1 g/mL, so that is roughly 80–100 g. Scrambled eggs with butter run about 150–200 kcal per 100 g. At about 90 g, that gives roughly 160 kcal.

